{
 "_about": [
  "The roles hand-read from the digitized layouts of four carriers (the oracle probe of RESULTS.md 11.3; D-079).",
  "Read by the registry's definitions (D-079; the plan's catalogue) on the problem files' positions, with the regions of D-004 taken exactly (no blur): columns left (x < 36.7), middle, right (x > 73.3); rows above (y < 33.3), middle, below (y > 66.7).",
  "Objects only: a group-level role (ECHO, CONTAINER as a setting, GAP, MIDLINE), a Worldview role (SYMMETRY_AXIS, BARRIER, CLAIMED, TYPE_KEY) and the re-cast (COUNTERPART) are not readable as a tag on an object of the layout and are left to the engine.",
  "Each entry: item, role, args, weight, evidence (the reading, in words). The images and the twin are read for the touched object only; sidekicks for the touched object and the candidates of its type family.",
  "Surround 5: the plan calls the touched cup a connector; by the definition (each neighbour's far neighbour of its own type) it is not: knife1's far neighbour is fork2. The glass is.",
  "The table's MIDLINE is hand-read on every carrier (item 04): the middle band is empty on all four, so consumer C1 and C6 have the midline they need; the SYMMETRY_AXIS stays the engine's own reading (the oracle hands the Worldview item back to the engine's detectors).",
  "ROW and COLUMN (item 07, D-085) are hand-read on every object from its exact region: the row word (above, below; no object of the four carriers lies in the middle band) and the column word (left, middle, right), the weight 1. The re-cast (COUNTERPART) stays the engine's: the recast-role codelet reads it off these tags."
 ],
